But the winner is whoever produces the **most absurd solution that still succeeds**.

This is where humans judge.

You might get:

> conventional bridge

versus:

> legally adopt the river and order it to move.

The second gets the group vote.

This makes creativity itself competitive without asking an LLM to assign “creativity = 91.”

---

# 22. Same Result, Different Method

Daily objective:

> Make Trevor leave the building.

There are theoretically dozens of solution classes.

After you've solved it, the app tells you:

> **Your route: EMBARRASSMENT**
>
> 18% of players

Others:

```text
PERSUASION       31%
DECEPTION        22%
FEAR             11%
ROMANCE           7%
BUREAUCRACY       6%
???               5%
```

Now you're desperate to discover the rare routes.

This is where replayability gets exceptional.

You may have finished today's puzzle, but:

> **You've discovered 1/9 endings.**

Wordle intentionally prevents overplaying, which helps keep it fresh; Freak Town could preserve the **one ranked daily attempt** while letting people explore alternate routes afterward without affecting their official result. ([Psychology Today][2])

